    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "fact": "In Grable & Sons Metal Products, Inc. v. Darue Engineering & Manufacturing, the Supreme Court established that federal question jurisdiction exists under 28 U.S.C. § 1331 for state-law claims if the federal issue is actually disputed, substantial, and capable of resolution in federal court without disrupting the federal-state balance.",
